' 13. Admin manages a user (change role / suspend, audit log)
' Use cases: Edit user accounts, Manage user roles, Suspend user accounts, View audit log (Manage users) · Actor: Admin
' Secondary: the suspended Learner
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Chain of responsibility: authenticate → requireAdmin on every admin route (routes/admin.routes.ts,
'     middleware/admin.middleware.ts)
'   - Decorator: action() wraps the controller with shared error handling (utils/action.ts)
'   - Unit of work: the change and its audit log entries are one transaction, with row locks so two admins can never
'     remove the last active administrator between them (services/admin.service.ts updateUser, withTransaction)
'   - Repository: users and audit log SQL in repositories/user.repository.ts, audit-log.repository.ts
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 13 Admin manages a user
title 13. Admin manages a user (change role / suspend, audit log)
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor Admin
boundary "Admin web app" as AdminWeb
control "Middleware chain\n(authenticate → requireAdmin)" as MW
control "Admin controller" as Ctrl
control "Admin service" as Svc
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
boundary "Web app" as Web
actor Learner

Admin -> AdminWeb : open Users, search a name
AdminWeb -> MW : GET /api/admin/users?search=…
MW -> Repo : token valid? account is an active admin?
alt not an active admin
  MW --> AdminWeb : 403 "Administrator access is required."
end
MW -> Ctrl : listUsers()
Ctrl -> Repo : users matching the search (page)
Repo -> DB : SELECT …
Ctrl --> AdminWeb : users list

Admin -> AdminWeb : edit a user: role, status (suspend), username, email → Save
AdminWeb -> MW : PATCH /api/admin/users/:id
MW -> Ctrl : updateUser()
Ctrl -> Svc : updateUser(adminId, id, edit)
Svc -> Svc : valid username, email, role, status?
alt invalid
  Svc --> AdminWeb : 400 "Enter a valid username, email, role, and status."
else editing yourself and it would remove your admin access or suspend you
  Svc --> AdminWeb : 409 "You cannot remove your own administrator access…"
end
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Svc -> Repo : lock administrator changes; still an active admin?
  Svc -> Repo : lock the user's role and status
  alt user not found
    Svc --> AdminWeb : 404 "User not found."
  else the last active admin would lose access
    Svc --> AdminWeb : 409 "At least one active administrator must remain."
  end
  Svc -> Repo : update the account
  Repo -> DB : UPDATE users …
  alt username or email already used
    Svc --> AdminWeb : 409 "That username or email is already in use."
  end
  loop each change (suspended / reactivated, role changed, details changed)
    Svc -> Repo : audit log entry (admin, user, action, from → to)
    Repo -> DB : INSERT audit_log …
  end
end
Ctrl --> AdminWeb : updated user
AdminWeb -> AdminWeb : show the new role / status in the row

opt the learner was suspended
  Learner -> Web : any action (next request)
  Web -> MW : any /api request with the old token
  MW -> Repo : account status
  MW --> Web : 403 "This account is inactive"
  Web -> Web : show the error (signing in again is refused while suspended)
end

Admin -> AdminWeb : open Audit log
AdminWeb -> MW : GET /api/admin/audit-log?action=…&user=…
MW -> Ctrl : listAuditLog() (moderation controller)
Ctrl -> Repo : entries matching the filters (newest first)
Repo -> DB : SELECT …
Ctrl --> AdminWeb : entries
AdminWeb -> AdminWeb : show who changed what, and when
@enduml
